        {
          "id": "f082eeb7-a3ea-44e1-b321-10b08208a892",
          "name": "Amazon EC2 Auto Scaling GET_ Attach Load Balancers",
          "request": {
            "name": "Amazon EC2 Auto Scaling GET_ Attach Load Balancers",
            "description": {
              "content": "<note> <p>This API operation is superseded by <a>AttachTrafficSources</a>, which can attach multiple traffic sources types. We recommend using <code>AttachTrafficSources</code> to simplify how you manage traffic sources. However, we continue to support <code>AttachLoadBalancers</code>. You can use both the original <code>AttachLoadBalancers</code> API operation and <code>AttachTrafficSources</code> on the same Auto Scaling group.</p> </note> <p>Attaches one or more Classic Load Balancers to the specified Auto Scaling group. Amazon EC2 Auto Scaling registers the running instances with these Classic Load Balancers.</p> <p>To describe the load balancers for an Auto Scaling group, call the <a>DescribeLoadBalancers</a> API. To detach a load balancer from the Auto Scaling group, call the <a>DetachLoadBalancers</a> API.</p> <p>This operation is additive and does not detach existing Classic Load Balancers or target groups from the Auto Scaling group.</p> <p>For more information, see <a href=\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/autoscaling/ec2/userguide/autoscaling-load-balancer.html\">Use Elastic Load Balancing to distribute traffic across the instances in your Auto Scaling group</a> in the <i>Amazon EC2 Auto Scaling User Guide</i>.</p>",
              "type": "text/plain"
            },
            "url": {
              "path": [
                ""
              ],
              "hash": "Action=AttachLoadBalancers",
              "host": [
                "{{baseUrl}}"
              ],
              "query": [
                {
                  "disabled": false,
                  "key": "AutoScalingGroupName",
                  "value": "<string>",
                  "description": "(Required) The name of the Auto Scaling group."
                },
                {
                  "disabled": false,
                  "key": "LoadBalancerNames",
                  "value": "<string>",
                  "description": "(Required) The names of the load balancers. You can specify up to 10 load balancers."
                },
                {
                  "disabled": false,
                  "key": "LoadBalancerNames",
                  "value": "<string>",
